cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "CUDA-zkML / PCANI: GPU zero-knowledge proofs of neural-network inference with proof-cost-aware adaptive routing"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "George David"
    family-names: "Tsitlauri"
    affiliation: "Department of Informatics and Telecommunications, University of Thessaly"
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gdtsitlauri/cuda-zkml"
abstract: >-
  A CUDA Groth16 prover for zero-knowledge proofs of quantized neural-network inference on BN254, with
  proof-cost-aware adaptive inference (PCANI): one proof for the selected model of a cheap-to-expensive
  cascade. Statement v2 adds context-bound proofs against replay, exact ReLU with range proofs, native
  convolution, Poseidon-committed private models and inputs with in-circuit routing, batching and a
  Groth16 phase-2 MPC ceremony.
keywords: [zero-knowledge proofs, zkML, Groth16, CUDA, GPU, Poseidon, verifiable machine learning]
